net — the network interfaces

  net                    every interface: link, counters, address
  net wired up           enable the wired role, persistently
  net wired down         disable it
  net wired dhcp         clear any static claim; DHCP asks
  net wired static 192.0.2.50/24 gw 192.0.2.1 dns 192.0.2.1
                         claim an address; gw and dns are optional

Configuration goes through the settings store and applies at once: it
outlives the command, and `cfg net` shows what is recorded.

With no static claim, an enabled interface asks DHCP as soon as its
cable carries, and prints the address when it arrives.

  net -p <address>       one ARP probe beneath the stack; the next
                         `net` shows which machine answered
